{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C header file", "description": "This file defines the interface for a routing tree data structure used for pub/sub messaging with support for wildcards, instance IDs, and multiple routes per topic. It includes data structures for routes and topics, functions for creating, destroying, adding, removing, and querying routes and topics, as well as logging and resolution functionalities. It is part of a messaging framework supporting complex topic hierarchies and subscription models.", "external_files": ["rtList.h"], "external_methods": [], "published": ["rtRoutingTree_Create", "rtRoutingTree_Destroy", "rtRoutingTree_AddTopicRoute", "rtRoutingTree_GetTopicRoutes", "rtRoutingTree_GetRouteTopics", "rtRoutingTree_RemoveRoute", "rtRoutingTree_RemoveTopic", "rtRoutingTree_ResolvePartialPath", "rtRoutingTree_LogStats", "rtRoutingTree_LogTopicTree", "rtRoutingTree_LogRouteList"], "classes": [{"name": "rtTreeRoute", "description": "Represents a route with an associated route object and list of directly assigned topics."}, {"name": "rtTreeTopic", "description": "Represents a topic node in the routing tree, with references to parent, child topics, and associated routes."}, {"name": "_rtRoutingTree", "description": "Main data structure representing the routing tree, containing the root topic and list of all routes."}], "methods": [{"name": "rtRoutingTree_Create", "description": "Initializes a new routing tree."}, {"name": "rtRoutingTree_Destroy", "description": "Deallocates and cleans up the routing tree."}, {"name": "rtRoutingTree_AddTopicRoute", "description": "Adds a route to a specific topic within the tree."}, {"name": "rtRoutingTree_GetTopicRoutes", "description": "Retrieves all routes associated with a specific topic."}, {"name": "rtRoutingTree_GetRouteTopics", "description": "Retrieves all topics associated with a specific route."}, {"name": "rtRoutingTree_RemoveRoute", "description": "Removes a route and its associated topics from the tr